<node id="1217392" title="Re^3: Multiple Packages in a Module?" created="2018-06-25 16:45:10" updated="2018-06-25 16:45:10" _doctext_mode="strict"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;Actually, no. The equivalent would be &lt;c&gt;BEGIN { require test_v1; test_v1-&gt;import; }&lt;/c&gt;.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No, because I wrote "in the case you describe", which is that there is one file &lt;c&gt;test_v1.pm&lt;/c&gt; with two packages, &lt;c&gt;Foo&lt;/c&gt; and &lt;c&gt;Foo::Bar&lt;/c&gt; (no mention of a &lt;c&gt;package test_v1&lt;/c&gt;). The code I showed is the equivalent of splitting that one file into two (&lt;c&gt;Foo.pm&lt;/c&gt; and &lt;c&gt;Foo/Bar.pm&lt;/c&gt;) and &lt;c&gt;use&lt;/c&gt;ing them individually.&lt;/p&gt;
</doctext>
